{"page":169,"verses":[{"verse_key":"7:150","surah":7,"ayah":150,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِۦ غَضْبَـٰنَ أَسِفًا قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُونِى مِنۢ بَعْدِىٓ ۖ أَعَجِلْتُمْ أَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۖ وَأَلْقَى ٱلْأَلْوَاحَ وَأَخَذَ بِرَأْسِ أَخِيهِ يَجُرُّهُۥٓ إِلَيْهِ ۚ قَالَ ٱبْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱسْتَضْعَفُونِى وَكَادُوا۟ يَقْتُلُونَنِى فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِىَ ٱلْأَعْدَآءَ وَلَا تَجْعَلْنِى مَعَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"On his return to his people, angry and aggrieved, Moses said, ‘How foul and evil is what you have done in my absence! Were you so keen to bring your Lord’s judgement forward?’ He threw the tablets down and seized his brother by the hair, pulling him towards him. Aaron said, ‘Son of my mother, these people overpowered me! They almost killed me! Do not give my enemies reason to rejoice! Do not include me with these evildoers!’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَمَّا","en_gloss":"And when","transliteration":"walammā","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":2,"ar":"رَجَعَ","en_gloss":"returned","transliteration":"rajaʿa","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مُوسَىٰٓ","en_gloss":"Musa","transliteration":"mūsā","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":4,"ar":"إِلَىٰ","en_gloss":"to","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":5,"ar":"قَوْمِهِۦ","en_gloss":"his people ","transliteration":"qawmihi","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":6,"ar":"غَضْبَـٰنَ","en_gloss":"angry","transliteration":"ghaḍbāna","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":7,"ar":"أَسِفًۭا","en_gloss":"and grieved","transliteration":"asifan","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":8,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"he said","transliteration":"qāla","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":9,"ar":"بِئْسَمَا","en_gloss":"Evil is what","transliteration":"bi'samā","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":10,"ar":"خَلَفْتُمُونِى","en_gloss":"you have done in my place","transliteration":"khalaftumūnī","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مِنۢ","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"7:150"},{"pos":12,"ar":"بَعْدِىٓ ۖ"