{"pos":16,"ar":"١٥٤","en_gloss":"(154)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"7:154"}]},{"verse_key":"7:155","surah":7,"ayah":155,"ar_uthmani":"وَٱخْتَارَ مُوسَىٰ قَوْمَهُۥ سَبْعِينَ رَجُلًا لِّمِيقَـٰتِنَا ۖ فَلَمَّآ أَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلرَّجْفَةُ قَالَ رَبِّ لَوْ شِئْتَ أَهْلَكْتَهُم مِّن قَبْلُ وَإِيَّـٰىَ ۖ أَتُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَّآ ۖ إِنْ هِىَ إِلَّا فِتْنَتُكَ تُضِلُّ بِهَا مَن تَشَآءُ وَتَهْدِى مَن تَشَآءُ ۖ أَنتَ وَلِيُّنَا فَٱغْفِرْ لَنَا وَٱرْحَمْنَا ۖ وَأَنتَ خَيْرُ ٱلْغَـٰفِرِينَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Moses chose from his people seventy men for Our appointment, and when they were seized by trembling, he prayed, ‘My Lord, if You had chosen to do so, You could have destroyed them long before this, and me too, so will You now destroy us for what the foolish among us have done? This is only a trial from You- through it, You cause whoever You will to stray and guide whoever You will- and You are our Protector, so forgive us and have mercy on us. You are the best of those who forgive.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَٱخْتَارَ","en_gloss":"And chose","transliteration":"wa-ikh'tāra","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":2,"ar":"مُوسَىٰ","en_gloss":"Musa","transliteration":"mūsā","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":3,"ar":"قَوْمَهُۥ","en_gloss":"(from) his people","transliteration":"qawmahu","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":4,"ar":"سَبْعِينَ","en_gloss":"seventy","transliteration":"sabʿīna","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":5,"ar":"رَجُلًۭا","en_gloss":"men","transliteration":"rajulan","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":6,"ar":"لِّمِيقَـٰتِنَا ۖ","en_gloss":"for Our appointment","transliteration":"limīqātinā","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":7,"ar":"فَلَمَّآ","en_gloss":"Then when","transliteration":"falammā","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":8,"ar":"أَخَذَتْهُمُ","en_gloss":"seized them","transliteration":"akhadhathumu","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱلرَّجْفَةُ","en_gloss":"the earthquake","transliteration":"l-rajfatu","verse_key":"7:155"},{"pos":10,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"he said",